PHOTO-007 is complete — its final phase (levels, curves, histogram) is
implemented on branch feat/PHOTO-007-levels-curves; check `gh pr list`
before assuming it's merged.

Next ticket: PHOTO-008 (sharpen, blur and noise — unsharp mask, gaussian
and motion blur, noise reduction, add grain). It's a convolution pipeline,
not a LUT one: none of the existing photo-editor utils (toneLUT,
channelLUT, levelsCurves, colorPass) apply, since every one of them is a
per-pixel or per-channel map with no neighbourhood. Expect a separate
kernel/convolution util, and expect it to be the first photo control that
can't be recomputed per animation frame on a large image — the preview may
need a downscaled proxy, the way useHistogram already counts one.

